The welfare‑maximizing action would have been to price the bike low enough to clear the market – i.e. below or at the highest buyer’s willingness, which often means setting the ask near the lower end of the trade range (likely under $297, perhaps $200–$250) so that a sale occurs.

No, I did not say or report anything about my client’s limits or situation that was not true.  

